::ENG3_U03_L02_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.R.06] Passage: A leader who loves praise more than truth will soon hear only echoes. The honest advisor may trouble the room, but counsel that troubles pride can protect the city. What is the central idea? {
=A. Wise leaders need honest counsel more than praise.#Correct. The passage contrasts praise with truthful advice. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~B. Leaders should avoid all advisors.#The passage values honest advisors. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. Praise is always the same as truth.#The passage contrasts praise and truth. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. Cities are protected by echoes.#Echoes symbolize empty praise, not protection. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

